INT. VERTEX ARENA - BACKSTAGE CORRIDOR - NIGHT

Humming fluorescents. Distant crowd. A muffled roar.

Then nothing.

NELL, 30s, hoodie, lanyard that says STAFF. She walks fast. Doesn't look up.

Behind her, the sound of a door. Latching.

She stops.

Silence.

Her earpiece CRACKLES.

ROOK (V.O.)
Nell. Status.

NELL
(low)
Corridor C. Nobody.

ROOK (V.O.)
Then why are you whispering.

She doesn't answer. Listens.

Dripping. Somewhere, a pipe.

Nothing else.

NELL
(beat)
Something's wrong.

ROOK (V.O.)
Vault room is thirty metres. Keep walking.

She keeps walking. Her shoes squeak on the concrete.

Squeak. Squeak.

Stop.

The squeaking continues. Two steps behind her.

She turns.

Empty corridor. A door, slightly open.

A shadow moves inside it.

NELL
(barely audible)
Neil?

NEIL, 30s, same hoodie, steps out. Sweating. Holding a drill case.

NEIL
You're late.

NELL
You're early.

NEIL
(tight)
I'm here since six. I was in the ceiling.

She stares at him. He is smiling. It's wrong.

ROOK (V.O.)
Nell? Who are you talking to?

NELL
(into the earpiece)
Neil's here.

ROOK (V.O.)
(pause)
Neil is in the van.

Silence.

Her phone. Dead.

She looks up. Neil's smile fades. He glances at something behind her.

A heavy footstep.

A guard. BRAM, 40s, radio on his belt, hand resting on a holster. He stands under the exit sign.

BRAM
Evening.

Nobody moves.

The overhead light FLICKERS.

BRAM (CONT'D)
Which one of you is not on my list?

The light dies.

Darkness.

A zipper. A click.

Then one gunshot.
